BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:RUSUNUNGUKO (liberty / independence / freedom)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20240411
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270626
DTSTAMP:20261003T150235Z
UID:34603b5d23c7006d137db55ad880@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Designer and visual artist Nontsikelelo Mutiti is the assistan
 t professor and director of graduate studies in graphic design at the Yale
  School of Art. Mutiti’s printed works\, films\, and installations engag
 e with the history and aesthetics of hair braiding in black life. “Ruka
 ” (Shona for “to weave\, braid\, or knit”) brings social binding alo
 ngside physical braiding\; the arrangements of salons\, living rooms\, and
  porches where hair is braided provide social contexts for her projects.\n
 \nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/rusununguko-liberty-independence-free
 dom
LOCATION:The Dome Gallery | Yale Schwarzman Center\, 168 Grove Street\, Ne
 w Haven CT\, 06511
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/rusununguko-liberty-independence-freedom
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Downtown Mystic Ghost Tours
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTSTAMP:20261003T150235Z
UID:84b25dc48e9bfb13f9ce1fcdc754@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Our Original Ghost Walk takes travelers through the historic d
 owntown Mystic landscape crossing the bascule bridge between both sides of
  the Mystic River\, guests will become immersed in the dark\, sordid and s
 upernatural history of New England’s famous seafaring village. From 17th
  century strife of colonial life amidst the Pequot Wars and the King Phill
 ip’s war to mysterious turn of the century murders\, Mystic’s history 
 was founded in darkness. As the centuries grew\, lost seafarers\, creepy c
 ryptids\, and scandalous happenings took place in our quaint seaside commu
 nity.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
LOCATION:Liberty Pole Square\, East Main Street\, Holmes Street\, Mystic C
 T\, 06355
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/downtown-mystic-ghost-tours-1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:America250: THE REAL REVOLUTION
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260501
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20271202
DTSTAMP:20261003T150235Z
UID:d496508c04ff23629e29f741202e@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:A mother with sons on opposing side of a life-changing conflic
 t. Enslaved men risking their lives for freedom. A woman posing as a man i
 n the fight for liberty. These are just a few of the people who are explor
 ed in The Real Revolution\, Westport Museum’s 2026 exhibit honoring the 
 250th anniversary of the founding of the nation. The exhibit delves into t
 he untold stories of the people who lived through the life-changing events
  of war and nation building. The exhibition includes an interactive playro
 om for kids\, and a tavern room in which special events will be held.\n\nS
 ource: https://ctvisit.com/events/america250-real-revolution
LOCATION:Westport Museum For History And Culture\, 25 Avery Place\, Westpo
 rt CT\, 06880
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/america250-real-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Norwich Stories of the American Revolution
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20280101
DTSTAMP:20261003T150235Z
UID:c5d13aef0c36e1820a30a1a8eed9@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:Norwich\, Connecticut was a center of Revolutionary activity i
 n Eastern Connecticut. From bands of Sons of Liberty to dedicated soldiers
  of all backgrounds\, the city produced scores of men and women who served
  in all capacities. From humble militiamen to a Signer of the Declaration 
 of Independence\, come and learn the lesser-known stories of these valiant
  Patriots as well as the story of America’s most infamous traitor\, Bene
 dict Arnold.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-america
 n-revolution
LOCATION:Slater Memorial Museum\, 108 Crescent Street\, Norwich CT\, 06360
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/norwich-stories-american-revolution
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sharks Exhibition
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260509
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270101
DTSTAMP:20261003T150235Z
UID:e900bdd06c9878548021b8ca7c6d@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:People have been fascinated by sharks for as long as we have e
 xplored the ocean\, and now the Connecticut Science Center is bringing tha
 t fascination to life in the limited-time exhibition\, Sharks. This immers
 ive experience brings you face-to-face with some of the ocean’s most fas
 cinating predators through full-scale shark models\, interactive experienc
 es\, underwater environments\, ancient fossils\, immersive media\, and —
  of course — a lot of teeth.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/shark
 s-exhibition
LOCATION:Connecticut Science Center\, 250 Columbus Boulevard\, Hartford CT
 \, 06103
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/sharks-exhibition
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Uncovering New London” History Tours in Celebration of Americ
 a 250
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260522
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTSTAMP:20261003T150235Z
UID:7b05ac2e6c98cc2886a522babef2@ctvisit-calendar
DESCRIPTION:In celebration of America’s 250th anniversary\, Uncovering N
 ew London Tours invites residents and visitors to explore the city’s ric
 h history through engaging guided walking and bus tours. Discover New Lond
 on’s role in the American Revolution\, its whaling heritage\, Black hist
 ory\, Gilded Age influence\, and hidden gems\, brought to life by knowledg
 eable local docents. Tours are available for groups of all sizes\, and can
  be customized to fit any schedule\, with optional stops and dining experi
 ences. A unique and immersive way to experience the stories that shaped th
 e Whaling City.\n\nSource: https://ctvisit.com/events/uncovering-new-londo
 n-history-tours-celebration-america-250
LOCATION:Downtown New London\, 27 Water St\, New London CT\, 06320
URL:https://ctvisit.com/events/uncovering-new-london-history-tours-celebra
 tion-america-250
END:VEVENT
